  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Architecture Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on whether this is best approached as a full-stack or client-side application, weighing the options based on the prompt\'s mention of Firebase services. I\'m exploring whether we can leverage standard client-side state with a localStorage fallback, or if a more robust architecture is required to meet requirements such as preventing duplicate registrations using email and mobile number.\n\n\n**Integrating Firebase Database**\n\nOkay, I\'m now fully committed to integrating Firebase Firestore. The user explicitly requested Firebase services, so I\'m investigating how to best provision a database. Crucially, I\'m leaning towards an approach that prioritizes immediate functionality within the iframe. I\'m imagining a robust client-side storage solution with optional Firebase sync, providing instant operation with local persistence. Furthermore, I\'m planning an admin dashboard with QR scanning, manual check-in, and export capabilities.\n\n\n**Confirming Client-Side Focus**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that a client-side React SPA is the optimal approach, aligning with the guidelines. Now, I am planning a fully optimized, browser-based solution that leverages localStorage as a \"mock\" database, allowing for instant loading and offline functionality. The user can register, view tickets, scan QR codes, use an admin dashboard, check-in, and view graphs without a complex backend, ensuring robust functionality even if Firebase isn\'t immediately provisioned.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Package Choices**\n\nI\'m now determining which packages to install. Considering the need for QR code generation, confetti, and analytics, I\'m leaning toward creating custom SVG charts rather than using Recharts, to avoid any potential React 19 compatibility issues and ensure complete control over the visual style. This approach maximizes reliability, customization, and seamless integration with the theme. I\'m also planning to use `qrcode` or a canvas-based library for the TECHCON Entry Pass QR code generation and `canvas-confetti` for register success!\n\n\n**Evaluating Skill Availability**\n\nI\'m now determining whether to read the `firebase-integration` skill or stick with a local persistent database. I\'m exploring the skill directory structure and checking for the skill\'s existence, potentially looking at `/skills/system_skills/firebase-skill/SKILL.md`. I\'m evaluating client-side persistence for 100% reliability, especially for the preview iframe. First, let\'s update `metadata.json`. I\'ll set the app name to \"TECHCON \'26\" and description.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will read the firebase-integration skill instructions first to ensure alignment with our storage strategy and Firebase best practices."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 724120139
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
