  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Ticket Pass**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the `/src/components/TicketPass.tsx` file. The user wants a sleek, premium entry pass post-registration, akin to an Apple Wallet or airline boarding pass. Key design elements include a gradient border, rounded corners, and premium glass appearance. I need to figure out how to incorporate the data into a visually appealing format.\n\n\n**Defining Ticket Contents**\n\nI\'ve finalized the data points needed for the ticket: the TECHCON logo, attendee name and registration ID, the QR code (containing secure attendee info), venue, date, organizer, and category. I\'m also planning the buttons for functionality. The QR code will include the registration ID, name, phone, email, and a verification token. Scanning this will automatically mark attendance.\n\nI\'ve realized that the canvas is incredibly good to simulate a digital wallet ticket. It\'s fast, client-side, and results in a perfect image download!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/TicketPass.tsx` to handle the digital pass display. Styled like an Apple Wallet meets airline boarding pass, it features glassmorphism, gradient frames, and punch holes. It generates a secure QR code on load using the `qrcode` package. It also implements an automated high-resolution `<canvas>` rasterization exporter that lets the attendee download their ticket as a high-quality PNG. It also supports printing/PDF trigger and deep-linked WhatsApp sharing."
    thinking_duration {
