  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Admin Dashboard**\n\nOkay, the `TicketPass.tsx` component is done, it\'s quite elegant. Now, I\'m shifting focus to the Admin Dashboard, specifically `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`. I\'m starting by remembering the user\'s specific requests for the dashboard \342\200\223 the need for a secure login and the initial data visualizations. I\'ll need to figure out what data is required for \"Total Registrations\", \"Today\'s Registrations\", and \"Attendance\".\n\n\n**Refining Attendance Tracking**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a much clearer picture for the attendance tracking features. I\'m focusing on the QR scanner implementation now. I\'m thinking both a real-time camera stream for easy scanning and a \"manual ticket search/mock gate simulation\" are essential for complete reliability. These options should give volunteers flexibility while ensuring seamless check-ins. I am also working on export functionality!\n\n\n**Envisioning the Check-In Terminal**\n\nI\'m imagining the check-in terminal, and I\'m really excited about it. It can be more than just a scanner. We could have a manual input with a simulated viewfinder, an attendee search, and a datatable. Also, we could add District, Occupation, and Gender charts. Plus, a secure login with a passcode would make it feel really authentic and secure. I want to build a breathtaking `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`, with Tailwind CSS and custom SVGs!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`. It features a secure gatekeeper login wall (passcode `TECHCON2026`). Once logged in, the administrator or check-in volunteer can view visual analytics (SVG bar and ring charts for districts, roles, and gender distributions). It also provides a gate search/check-in station where they can scan ticket codes, search records, manually toggle check-ins, and export complete CSV spreadsheets."
    thinking_duration {
