    modified_response: "I have successfully built and verified the official, world-class interactive digital platform for **TECHCON \'26**. The application compiles perfectly without any linting or compilation warnings.\n\n### Design Concept & Aesthetic Frame\nThe digital experience of TECHCON \'26 has been crafted using a high-contrast **Slate-White & Deep Indigo** color language. It blends generous negative space with crisp, futuristic geometric lines to deliver an editorial-grade conference identity. The key design components of the platform include:\n\n*   **Introductory Preloader**: A fluid entrance animation featuring ribbon-like curves assembling slowly, accompanied by network nodes and a progress counter, before smoothly unlocking the main layout.\n*   **Interactive Circuit Canopy**: An ultra-thin branching canvas-drawn digital circuit background pulsing gently at a subtle opacity.\n*   **Sticky Glass Navigation**: An elegant navigation bar that dynamically triggers page-scrolling offsets and provides seamless shortcuts to check-in stations.\n*   **Immersive Hero Presentation**: Displays floating 3D-gradient logo geometries, live countdown clocks, and instant primary action buttons.\n*   **The Experience Timeline**: A vertically-aligned chronological rail detailing program keynotes, expert panels, drone workshops, and dining mixers with staggered animations.\n*   **Geographic Venue Transit**: An interactive schematics vector map of Cochin University of Science and Technology (CUSAT) coupled with clean transit descriptions and one-click deep-linking.\n*   **Instant Calendar Sync**: A dedicated calendar button allowing attendees to synchronize and lock the event\'s schedule into Google Calendar.\n*   **Secure Registrations**: A multi-step form wizard that validates registrations in real time, preventing duplicate profiles against local storage.\n*   **Digital Boarding Passes**: A premium Apple Wallet-style boarding pass complete with side cutouts, gradient frames, and a live secure QR code. Attendees can download their ticket as a high-resolution PNG image, print/export to PDF, or share registration credentials to WhatsApp.\n*   **Volunteer & Admin Console**: Locked behind a secure passcode (`TECHCON2026`), administrators can analyze district, age, and interest distributions through custom SVG charts. The panel also houses a search-and-check-in verifier terminal to scan and check in ticket holders instantly.\n"
