  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring CSS Architecture**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve just observed that `index.css` is surprisingly lean, relying entirely on Tailwind. This simplicity got me thinking. Turns out with Tailwind v4, defining custom theme variables is possible using `@theme` directly within the `index.css` file. I\'m now exploring potential font imports to see how this can be best implemented.\n\n\n**Importing Google Fonts**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed with importing specific Google Fonts directly into `index.css`. The goal is to establish a futuristic and tech-focused aesthetic, echoing the brand kit\'s visual language. After evaluating several options, I\'ve chosen Space Grotesk, Orbitron, and Inter for the desired visual weight. I\'ll need to define how they\'ll be applied across the project.\n\n\n**Defining Custom Colors**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the color palette, and I\'m adding JetBrains Mono, Rajdhani, and the provided color values to the custom theme variables. The plan is to create Tailwind classes for easy application, such as `text-brand-pink`, and `bg-brand-black` and so on, by defining these colors directly in the `@theme` directive, or as direct hex codes. It offers a lot of flexibility.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` to see how the logo is designed and styled, and adapt it to look exactly like the \"TECHCON 26\" brand kit."
