  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Preferences**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating the user\'s font preferences. I\'ve noted the request for Jura (`Jura Bold`) for headings and will import it from Google Fonts. I\'m checking `src/index.css` to verify the existing font import setup and identify where to integrate the Jura font.\n\n\n**Integrating New Fonts**\n\nI\'ve added the necessary Google Font import for Jura and also included Space Grotesk, Orbitron, Inter, JetBrains Mono, and Rajdhani. The Jura font will be mapped in `@theme` as `--font-jura`. I\'m now turning my attention to the hero section, specifically adjusting font sizes for \"techcon\" and \"26\" to be consistent and optimizing the mobile view. I\'m also revising the about section content.\n\n\n**Refining Brand Identity**\n\nI\'m now revising the \"About\" section, removing the mentorship description and adding \"Youth & Students Tech Ecosystem\" as a key point, linking it to the MSF Kerala State Committee. I\'m also preparing a \"Syllabus/Technology Sectors\" section above the sessions, incorporating icons and brief captions for clarity. The original \"syllabus & tracks\" section will be replaced with specific \"Sessions\" including AI Summit, workshops, and placement discussions.\n\n\n**Structuring Event Details**\n\nI\'m now restructuring the event information. I\'m focusing on creating a \"Sessions\" section to replace \"WhyAttend,\" and I\'m updating the syllabus/track sections to include an `athon and workshop for college students` section, followed by a `PRO NIGHT and Closing ceremony` and then an exhibition & fun games. I will refine the venue section, removing the extra tabs and providing concise details about the nearest transport options.\n\n\n**Defining Registration Fields**\n\nI\'m now outlining the registration form\'s structure. I\'ll include \"Place\" as a required field in the registration profile. I\'m dynamically adjusting the questions based on the selected role, with different fields for Students, Working Professionals, Entrepreneurs, Researchers, and Others. Mandatory fields will vary based on role selection, such as Institution and Level for students, and Job Title for professionals. I\'m streamlining the process by removing Stage 3 and adding a non-mandatory \"Technology Interests\" section. I\'m replacing Campus Schematic with Collaboration grounds, and visualizing with elegant graphics.\n\n\n**Implementing Registration Backend**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the registration backend. I\'m ensuring that after the user submits registration details, a ticket is instantly generated and saved. I\'m prioritizing duplicate prevention based on phone numbers, auto-filling existing data, and disabling the submit button with a warning. I\'m also planning to support this functionality in the frontend and backend, with the goal of creating a Google Apps Script code to sync with Google Sheets for secure, unhackable registration handling, duplicate prevention, and admin control. I will provide a clear guide and copyable code inside the application.\n\n\n**Generating Ticket IDs**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ticket generation. I\'ve designed the registration ID format to be sequential (TC26A001, etc.) and am working on the logic for elegant sequential generation. On successful registration, I\'ll prominently display the ID and include it on the ticket, alongside the participant\'s phone number.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 376798785
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
