  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding \"Place\" Field**\n\nI\'ve incorporated the user\'s explicit request to include a \"Place of Residence\" textbox. I\'m positioning it adjacent to the \"District\" or \"Personal\" information fields within the registration form\'s profile. I\'m confident this placement will provide the user with the flexibility and precision needed for data collection.\n\n\n**Refining Educational Data Collection**\n\nI\'m now revising the student section of the form. I\'ve removed the course, department, and year fields, focusing instead on \"Institution\" and \"Level.\" For \"Level,\" I\'ll offer a list: Primary, High School, Higher Secondary, UG, PG, Diploma, Professional courses, and \"Other.\" If the user selects UG, PG, or Professional courses, a follow-up textbox, \"Which course?\", will appear.\n\n\n**Streamlining Registration Steps**\n\nI\'ve significantly streamlined the registration process! I\'ve eliminated steps, reducing it to just two: Personal Profile and Role Selection with details. A submit button is now directly accessible on the second step. Upon submission, a ticket will be generated. This results in a much more efficient and user-friendly experience, removing the need for a preference or review step.\n\n\n**Implementing Mobile Number Check**\n\nI\'m now implementing the mobile number validation feature. On mobile number entry, I\'ll check our database (using `getRegistrations()`). If a duplicate is found, I\'ll set a state flag, auto-populate all other fields (name, email, etc.), disable the submit button, and display a warning message: \"This mobile number is already connected with a registered participant. Try another phone number.\" It\'s a great improvement!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 38
      nanos: 148230071
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
