  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the White Theme**\n\nOkay, so I\'m envisioning a crisp, white-themed admin dashboard. The background will be light off-white with defined borders, utilizing deep charcoal text. This will frame brightly-colored metric cards for visual appeal. I\'m focusing on the live dashboards for total registrations and gender-wise data. The challenge is to maintain clarity and readability within this white scheme.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Categories**\n\nI\'m now expanding the data categories visualized. I\'m incorporating category breakdowns for attendees (Student, Professional, etc.) and checking data (Attended vs. Not Attended). I\'ve got a detailed data table design with full attendee records and search functionality, alongside PDF and CSV export options. A refresh button will also be included. Crucially, I\'m designing a secure Google Apps Script for saving the data, including duplicate checks and authentication, which will be prominently displayed. I will be including a copyable script!\n\n\n**Implementing Security Protocols**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the secure data saving process. I\'m writing and testing a Google Apps Script to handle data submissions securely. Authorization, through a secret password, is critical, as is ensuring only authorized access. I\'m planning to use a `doPost` function that receives data, checks the passcode, and adds new entries or updates the Google Sheet accordingly. Error handling and success/failure messaging are being implemented.\n\n\n**Refining Data Validation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data validation within the Google Apps Script. I\'m focusing on incorporating checks for duplicate mobile numbers to prevent redundant entries in the spreadsheet. I\'m leveraging the existing rows of data to detect and reject submissions with matching mobile numbers, returning a specific error message. This will prevent data corruption and ensure data integrity.\n\n\n**Finalizing Script Integration**\n\nI\'ve just finalized the Google Apps Script integration. I\'m especially pleased with the error handling, which provides detailed success or failure messages in JSON format. The script handles incoming data, automatically formats timestamps, and includes course and professional information. I\'m focusing now on implementing and testing a robust, native PDF export functionality from the front-end, triggered by the `handleExportPDF()` function, that cleanly presents the data!\n\n\n**Designing the Admin Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now completely redesigning the admin dashboard with a gorgeous white theme. I\'m focusing on rendering clear statistics for total registrations, gender and category breakdowns, and a \"checked in vs not attended\" breakdown. I\'m building a searchable data table, including all fields, and adding refresh and export actions. A tab will display the secure, copy-pasteable Google Apps Script code with instructions. I\'m implementing a clean print stylesheet and renaming the CSV export to \"Export to Excel (CSV)\".\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 54
      nanos: 794798445
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
