  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have completed the specified enhancements for the **TECHCON \'26** application. All components build successfully and integrate seamlessly into the modern, high-contrast user interface.\n\n### Key Enhancements Implemented:\n\n1. **Futuristic Registration Form Restructuring (`RegistrationForm.tsx`)**:\n   - **Two-Step Wizard Optimization**: Condensed the registration process into 2 rapid steps, removing the secondary preferences step to maximize conversion rates.\n   - **Personalized Residence Information**: Added a required **Place of Residence** input field.\n   - **Role-Specific Parameters**: \n     - **Students**: Removed detailed years/courses and replaced with **Institution Name** and **Education Level** (`Primary`, `Highschool`, `Higher secondary`, `UG`, `PG`, `Diploma`, `Professional courses`, `others`). If `UG`, `PG`, or `Professional courses` is chosen, a conditional column appears asking \"Which Course?\".\n     - **Working Professionals**: Asks for **Job Title** and **Institution Name/Employer** (both optional).\n     - **Entrepreneurs**: Asks for **Company Name** and **Sector/Industry** (both optional).\n     - **Researchers**: Asks for **University** and **Department**.\n   - **Intelligent Duplicate Prevention & Auto-Fill**: On entering a mobile number, the system automatically checks the registration records. If a duplicate is found, it automatically retrieves and populates their credentials, disables the submit buttons, and presents an amber warning: *\"This mobile number is already connected with a registered participant. Try another phone number.\"*\n\n2. **White Theme Entry Pass System (`TicketPass.tsx` & `db.ts`)**:\n   - **Ticket Shape & Notches**: Rendered the ticket as a crisp, professional **White Theme Pass** with modern circular notch cuts on the side and a top header stripe of the brand gradient.\n   - **Horizontal Branding**: Displayed the horizontal **TECHCON \'26 by msf TechFed** logo on top.\n   - **Identifier Precision**: Generated unique registration IDs sequentially starting from **`TC26A001`** up to **`TC26A999`**, then rolling into **`TC26B001`**, etc.\n   - **Participant Display**: Clearly displays the participant\'s **Registration ID** and **Mobile Phone Number** directly under their name.\n   - **Simplified Actions**: Implemented a single **Save Entry Pass** button (saving high-quality custom canvas-drawn PNG cards) alongside a direct **Share Entry ID on WhatsApp** action.\n   - **Simplified Note**: Replaced the previous long instructions block with a crisp, welcoming note: *\"Please present this entry pass at the venue gate for instant check-in.\"*\n\n3. **White Theme Administrator Console & Sheet Sync (`AdminDashboard.tsx`)**:\n   - **White Theme Redesign**: Re-engineered the console with clean off-white canvas styling, high-contrast grey text, and vibrant color-coded metrics.\n   - **Live Telemetry Dashboards**: Provides interactive data visualization modules for **Total Registrations**, **Gender Demographics**, **Category-Wise Distribution**, and **Checked In vs Absentee Attendance Ratios**.\n   - **Complete Directory & Search**: Houses a fully filterable records table with an immediate search box.\n   - **Instant Data Actions**: Configured a **Refresh** button on top, **Export to Excel (CSV)**, and an elegant **Export to PDF** button that opens a pre-formatted print sheet of the current directory view.\n   - **Google Apps Script Storage Integration**: Provides a copy-pasteable, robust, and secure script block with instructions inside the dashboard to facilitate a secure pipeline directly to a Google Sheet, equipped with secure passphrase checks and server-side duplicate phone filtering.\n\n4. **Console Access & Header (`Navbar.tsx`)**:\n   - Added a clean **Console** action button in both desktop and mobile drawer headers to give organizers instant, seamless access to the gate console.\n\n5. **Bold Destination Venue (`Venue.tsx`)**:\n   - Replaced default tabs with clean, scannable transit cards for the nearest **Metro**, **Railway**, and **Airport** hubs, with distances clearly indicated in brackets.\n   - Highlighted the official location as **CUSAT, Kochi**, bolding the word **Kochi**.\n   - Swapped the scheduling campus diagram for a vibrant **Collaboration Grounds** layout highlighting alpha, beta, gamma, and delta student meetups."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
